  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contribution to IOM&#x2019;s Response to Pakistan Floods 2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ranked as the eighth most vulnerable country in the world to climate change, Pakistan is prone to natural hazards, which in recent years have become more recurrent, causing significant losses of lives and physical assets. Since mid-June 2022, Pakistan has endured extreme monsoon weather, causing widespread flooding and landslides that affected 33 million people in the country, with at least 664,000 people displaced.In response to the floods, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) is delivering lifesaving assistance to 132,300 flood-affected individuals &#x2013; mainly in Sindh, Balochistan and Khyber Pakhtunkhwa provinces &#x2013; while setting the foundation for early recovery and durable solutions. This involves the provision of multi-sectoral assistance and reinforcement of evidence-based responses through the wider availability of reliable data produced by IOM&#x2019;s Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) on the mobility trends and needs of floods-displaced populations.</narrative>
  </description>
